---
description: Test rules and strict xfails
globs: tests/**
alwaysApply: false
---
- Run with `pytest` (testpaths = `tests`). Tests are network-free (fixture source + `tests/golden/`).
- Never weaken, skip or delete a test. Every `xfail(strict=True)` documents a real defect
  (see its `reason=`). It may only be removed in the same commit that fixes that defect, with the
  fix recorded in `CHANGES.md` (as engine-v1.3 did for the score-range defect). If one XPASSes
  unexpectedly, report it — don't delete the marker.
- The suite is expected to be fully green on a clean clone. Any failure is a regression.
- Journal tests use synthetic fixtures in `tests/golden/journal/` via the `golden_journal` fixture
  (`tests/conftest.py`). Never copy real `data/journal/` files into the repo — it is public.
- Tests that depend on today's date must pin the clock (patch `_today_et` or equivalent);
  hard-coded expiry dates otherwise turn into failures once they pass.
- `test_journal_metrics.py::test_live_journal_concat_fifo_expected_totals` checks the owner's live
  journal and skips when it's absent. It's a data-integrity check; don't make it pass by editing thresholds.
- Guards are tested against real captures in `tests/golden/`, not synthetic data.
- New tests must not read `data/` or the network. Put fixtures in `tests/golden/`.
